  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Fix: a resistor lead can't join a MIDI jack header-pin directly. I added two hook-up wires, wire4 (R1 to MIDI pin 4) and wire5 (R2 to MIDI pin 5), so step 1 had two parts too few. The tutorial lists 'hook-up wires' without a count.",
   "The schematic wires everything directly with no breadboard, so none is used.",
   "Connections: MIDI pin 5 goes through R2 (220 ohm) to Uno D1 (TX). MIDI pin 2 goes to GND. MIDI pin 4 goes through R1 (220 ohm) to 5V. MIDI pins 1 and 3 are unused.",
   "The tutorial doesn't say how the wires attach to the resistors and jack. I assumed soldered joints at the resistor leads and jack pins, and wire ends pushed into the Uno header sockets."
  ]
 },
